CoincidentRootLocus -- the class of all coincident root loci
************************************************************

Description
===========

The coincident root locus associated with a partition
$\lambda=(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_d)$ of a number $n$ is the closed subvariety
of the projective space $\mathbb{P}^n = \mathbb{P}(Sym^n(K^2))$ given by binary
forms that factor as ${L_1}^{\lambda_1}\cdots{L_d}^{\lambda_d}$ for some linear
forms $L_1,\ldots,L_d$ over $\bar{K}$. For instance, if
$\lambda=(2,1,\ldots,1)$, then we have the classical discriminant hypersurface;
in the opposite case, if $\lambda=(n)$ we have the rational normal curve of
degree $n$.

See also
========

  * *note coincidentRootLocus: coincidentRootLocus, -- makes a coincident root
    locus

