polarDegrees -- polar degrees of a coincident root locus
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polarDegrees X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note coincident root locus: CoincidentRootLocus,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the polar degrees of X

Description
===========

This method is based on a conjecture given in Algebraic boundaries among
typical ranks for real binary forms of arbitrary degree (see
https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.01958 ), which has been verified for all the
coincident root loci $X\subset\mathbb{P}^r$ with $r\leq 7$.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : X = coincidentRootLocus(3,2,2)|
|                                   |
|o1 = CRL(3,2,2)                    |
|                                   |
|o1 : Coincident root locus         |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : polarDegrees X                |
|                                   |
|o2 = {36, 80, 66, 24}              |
|                                   |
|o2 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+

