realrank -- compute the real rank
*********************************

  * Usage: 
        realrank F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a binary form
        $F\in K[x,y]$ of degree $d$, where $K$ is either $\mathbb{Q}$ or a
        polynomial ring over $\mathbb{Q}$ (currently, with only one variable)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Limit: realrank_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, set a bound for the rank
      * *note QepcadOptions: QepcadOptions, => ..., default value
        (20000000,10000), set the number of cells in the garbage collected
        space
      * *note Range: realrank_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRange=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value (-infinity,infinity), can be assigned an interval
      * *note Verbose: realrank_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, request verbose feedback
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the real rank of $F$, i.e., the
        minimum integer $r$ such that there is a decomposition $F =
        c_1\,(l_1)^d+\cdots+c_r\,(l_r)^d$ where $l_1,\ldots,l_r$ are real
        linear forms and $c_1,\ldots,c_r\in\mathbb{R}$

Description
===========

This method requires generally the program QEPCAD (see
https://www.usna.edu/CS/qepcadweb/B/QEPCAD.html ) to be installed. Source code
and installation instructions for it are available at Downloading and
Installing QEPCAD (see https://www.usna.edu/CS/qepcadweb/INSTALL/IQ.html ).

Below we compute the real rank of a binary form of degree 7.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R := QQ[x,y];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = 2*x^7+7*x^6*y+168*x^5*y^2+140*x^4*y^3+70*x^3*y^4+21*x^2*y^5+56*x*y^6|
|                                                                             |
|       7     6        5 2       4 3      3 4      2 5        6     7         |
|o2 = 2x  + 7x y + 168x y  + 140x y  + 70x y  + 21x y  + 56x*y  + 4y          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QQ[x..y]                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|+4*y^7                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : realrank F                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 5                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the case when the coefficient ring $K$ contains a variable, say $u$, then
the method returns a value $r$ if the real rank of $F$ is $r$ for all the real
values of $u$ in the range specified by the option *note
realrank(...,Range=>...): realrank_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRange=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,. An error
is thrown if the answer is not uniform.

+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : Ru := QQ[u][x,y];                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = u*x^4*y+2*x^2*y^3            |
|                                      |
|        4      2 3                    |
|o5 = u*x y + 2x y                     |
|                                      |
|o5 : QQ[u][x..y]                      |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : realrank(F,Range=>(0,infinity))  |
|                                      |
|o6 = 3                                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : realrank(F,Range=>[-1,0])        |
|                                      |
|o7 = 3                                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : realrank(F,Range=>(-infinity,-1))|
|                                      |
|o8 = 3                                |
+--------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note complexrank: complexrank, -- compute the complex rank

