singularLocus(CoincidentRootLocus) -- the singular locus of a coincident root locus
***********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note singularLocus: (Macaulay2Doc)singularLocus,
  * Usage: 
        singularLocus X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note coincident root locus: CoincidentRootLocus,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of coincident root loci such
        that their union coincides with the singular locus of X

Description
===========

The singular locus of a coincident root locus is the union of certain subloci,
as described in the paper by J. Chipalkatti - On equations defining coincident
root loci - J. Algebra 267, 246-271, 2003; see also the paper by S. Kurmann -
Some remarks on equations defining coincident root loci - J. Algebra 352,
223-231, 2012.

